<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yu County, Hebei</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yuxian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yu County, or Yuxian, is a county in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhangjiakou">Zhangjiakou</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, in an upland basin near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a> border. It occupies the area of ancient Dai, a state of the Di peoples conquered by Zhao in the fifth century BCE, and later the seat of the kingdoms and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commandery">commanderies</a> of Dai on the northern frontier. It is noted for its walled town and traditional paper-cutting.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yu-county-hebei.jpg" alt="Yu County, Hebei" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Wangyunfeng at Chinese Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%94%9A%E5%8E%BF%E5%9C%A8%E5%BC%A0%E5%AE%B6%E5%8F%A3%E5%B8%82%E7%9A%84%E4%BD%8D%E7%BD%AE.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
